{
  "slug": "okr-writing",
  "concept": "OKR Writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "OKRs (Objectives and Key Results) are a goal-setting framework. The form is deceptively simple — one inspirational Objective, three to five measurable Key Results — but most OKRs in the wild are broke",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "OKRs (Objectives and Key Results) are a goal-setting framework. The form is deceptively simple - one inspirational Objective, three to five measurable Key Results - but most OKRs in the wild are broken. They are project plans wearing OKR clothing.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The Objective is qualitative, inspirational, time-bound.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Each Key Result is measurable - a numerator over a denominator, by a date.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The KR measures an outcome (value delivered), not an output (work done) and never an input (effort spent).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. The measurable-KR test: numerator, denominator, deadline",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every KR must answer:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#2-the-measurable-kr-test-numerator-denominator-deadline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Numerator - what is being counted?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#2-the-measurable-kr-test-numerator-denominator-deadline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Denominator - relative to what?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#2-the-measurable-kr-test-numerator-denominator-deadline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Deadline - by when?",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#2-the-measurable-kr-test-numerator-denominator-deadline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Fails: \"Improve onboarding.\" (no numerator, no denominator, no deadline)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#2-the-measurable-kr-test-numerator-denominator-deadline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Fails: \"Reach 1000 users.\" (no denominator, no deadline)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#2-the-measurable-kr-test-numerator-denominator-deadline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Passes: \"Grow week-1 activation rate from 28% to 45% by 2026-09-30.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#2-the-measurable-kr-test-numerator-denominator-deadline",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. OKR vs KPI — different jobs",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "KPI (Key Performance Indicator) - a steady-state health metric you watch all the time. KPIs run forever.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#3-okr-vs-kpi-different-jobs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "OKR - a change goal for a bounded period. Says \"we are choosing to push this number from X to Y this quarter.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#3-okr-vs-kpi-different-jobs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A KPI can become a KR if you decide to push it - but the KR must specify the from-to delta and the deadline.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#3-okr-vs-kpi-different-jobs",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Input → Output → Outcome hierarchy",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Input - effort, headcount, money spent. (\"hired 5 engineers\") - never a KR.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#4-input-output-outcome-hierarchy",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Output - work produced, artifacts shipped. (\"shipped the new dashboard\") - almost never a KR.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#4-input-output-outcome-hierarchy",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Outcome - change in the world, value delivered. (\"dashboard adoption reached 60% of paying teams\") - this is what KRs measure.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#4-input-output-outcome-hierarchy",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Felipe Castro's \"so what?\" test: read the KR and ask \"so what?\" If the answer is another metric (the outcome), the original was an output.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#4-input-output-outcome-hierarchy",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Ambitious-but-not-impossible: the 70% rule",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "For aspirational / stretch OKRs:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#5-ambitious-but-not-impossible-the-70-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Pick a target where your confidence of hitting 100% is about 5 out of 10 (50/50 at draft time).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#5-ambitious-but-not-impossible-the-70-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Score around 0.7 on average at the end of the quarter is healthy.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#5-ambitious-but-not-impossible-the-70-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Consistently scoring 1.0 means you sandbagged. Scoring < 0.4 means you set fantasy targets.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#5-ambitious-but-not-impossible-the-70-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "For committed OKRs (operational must-haves - SLAs, compliance deadlines), the target is 1.0 and anything less is a problem.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#5-ambitious-but-not-impossible-the-70-rule",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. The rollup pattern across org levels",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Company sets 3–5 Objectives for the quarter.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#6-the-rollup-pattern-across-org-levels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Each team picks ~3 Objectives that contribute to the company set.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#6-the-rollup-pattern-across-org-levels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "An individual contributor may have 1–2 personal Objectives that map to a team Objective.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#6-the-rollup-pattern-across-org-levels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Key insight: roughly half of OKRs should be set bottom-up. Pure top-down OKRs kill engagement.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#6-the-rollup-pattern-across-org-levels",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Mid-quarter check-in: traffic-light language",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Green - on track, no help needed.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#7-mid-quarter-check-in-traffic-light-language",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Yellow - at risk, here is what would unblock me.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#7-mid-quarter-check-in-traffic-light-language",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Red - will not hit current target. Either re-plan or formally revise the KR.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#7-mid-quarter-check-in-traffic-light-language",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. End-of-cycle scoring (0.0 to 1.0)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "For each KR, compute the actual / target on its native scale:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#8-end-of-cycle-scoring-00-to-10",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Started at 28%, target 45%, ended at 38%. Progress = (38 − 28) / (45 − 28) = 10/17 ≈ 0.59.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#8-end-of-cycle-scoring-00-to-10",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9. Common bad-OKR patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "\"Ship feature X by date Y\" - that is a task, not a KR. The KR is the outcome the feature is supposed to produce.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#9-common-bad-okr-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Do our normal job well\" - operational baselines are KPIs, not OKRs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#9-common-bad-okr-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Activity counts - \"publish 12 blog posts\" measures effort, not outcome.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#9-common-bad-okr-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Sandbagged targets - KRs you are 95% confident in.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#9-common-bad-okr-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Too many KRs - more than 5 per Objective is a wishlist.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#9-common-bad-okr-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Set-and-forget - OKRs scored only at quarter end.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/okr-writing/#9-common-bad-okr-patterns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "References",
      "facts": [
